#DESCRIPTION
Intrinsic magnetic field: dipole and crustal field together, the crustal part
from a spherical harmonic file (BATSRUS layout, three header lines + 'n m
value' triples).

Same isolated setup as the dipole deck: SOLVEEM F and a zero UNIFORMSTATE
field, so the only field in the domain is the static intrinsic field B0. The
validator checks that B0 equals the sum of the dipole-only deck and the
crustal-only deck, i.e. that the two static fields superpose linearly.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-4.0                    xMin   [code units: 1 unit = 1 planetary radius]
 4.0                    xMax
-4.0                    yMin
 4.0                    yMax
-2.0                    zMin   four cells so that z = 0 is a node
 2.0                    zMax   plane and the body fits inside

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
32                      nCellY
4                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
4                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
0.04                    mass           Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [/cc]   Species 0: ions
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
1.0e4                   T [K]
5.0                     rho [/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
1.0e4                   T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#PLANETRADIUS
1.0e5                   radius [m]

Same orientation as the dipole + body deck: theta = 90 and phi = 180 put the
dipole axis along +x, inside the plane the plot writes.
#DIPOLE
100.0                   strength [nT]
90.0                    theta [deg]
180.0                   phi [deg]
-1.0                    rRef [m, <0 = take it from the body/planet radius]

#CRUSTALFIELD
crustal_nm2.txt         fileName
